# Clerk Billing Standards

This project uses **Clerk Billing** for all subscription and payment handling. Never use Stripe directly or any other payment library.

## Available Plans

- `free_user` — default free tier
- `pro` — paid plan

## Available Features

- `3_deck_limit` — limits user to 3 decks (free tier)
- `unlimited_decks` — no deck limit (pro tier)
- `ai_flashcard_generation` — AI card generation (pro tier)

## Checking Access — Server Components

Use `has()` from `auth()` on the server side:

```tsx
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server'

export default async function Page() {
  const { has } = await auth()

  const isPro = has({ plan: 'pro' })
  const canUseAI = has({ feature: 'ai_flashcard_generation' })
  const hasUnlimitedDecks = has({ feature: 'unlimited_decks' })
}
```

## Checking Access — Client Components / JSX

Use the `<Show>` component with a `fallback` for gating UI:

```tsx
import { Show } from '@clerk/nextjs'

<Show
  when={{ feature: 'unlimited_decks' }}
  fallback={<p>Upgrade to Pro for unlimited decks.</p>}
>
  <CreateDeckButton />
</Show>
```

## Pricing Page

Use the `<PricingTable />` component on a dedicated `/pricing` page:

```tsx
import { PricingTable } from '@clerk/nextjs'

export default function PricingPage() {
  return (
    <div style={{ maxWidth: '800px', margin: '0 auto', padding: '0 1rem' }}>
      <PricingTable />
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Rules

- **NEVER** implement custom subscription logic, paywalls, or payment flows outside of Clerk Billing
- **NEVER** call Stripe APIs directly — Clerk handles payment processing
- Always use `has({ plan: '...' })` or `has({ feature: '...' })` — not custom flags or DB fields
- Gate features using `has()` in Server Components or `<Show>` in Client Components
- Redirect unauthenticated users to `/` before checking billing access
